{"name":"Tatarian Aster","hex":"#976e9a","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"aster","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of several plants of the genus Aster; one of its flowers.","A star-shaped structure formed during the mitosis of a cell."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/aster"}],"entries":[{"title":"Aster tataricus","blocks":[{"text":"Aster tataricus, also called Tatarian aster and Tatarinow's aster, is a member of the Aster genus of flowering plants native to East Asia."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/Aster_Tataricus.JPG/330px-Aster_Tataricus.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aster_tataricus"},{"title":"Aster (genus)","blocks":[{"text":"Aster is a genus of perennial flowering plants in the family Asteraceae. Its circumscription has been narrowed, and it now encompasses around 170 species, all but one of which are restricted to Eurasia; many species formerly in Aster are now in other genera of the tribe Astereae. Aster amellus is the type species of the genus and the family Asteraceae."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/Asteraceae_-_Aster_amellus.JPG/330px-Asteraceae_-_Aster_amellus.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aster_(genus)"},{"title":"Permian","blocks":[{"text":"The Permian is a geologic period and stratigraphic system which spans 47 million years, from the end of the Carboniferous Period 298.9 Ma to the beginning of the Triassic Period 251.902 Ma. It is the sixth and last period of the Paleozoic Era; the following Triassic Period belongs to the Mesozoic Era. The concept of the Permian was introduced in 1841 by geologist Sir Roderick Murchison, who named it after the region of Perm in Russia."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/Mollweide_Paleographic_Ma